-### SUDS
-SUDS is a 4D radiance field representation designed for large-scale dynamic urban scenes that factorizes the scene into three separate multi-resolution hash table structures: static, dynamic, and far-field [14964-suds.md]. It enables free-viewpoint rendering, semantic decomposition, and 3D scene flow estimation using only unlabeled inputs (RGB, sparse LiDAR, 2D descriptors, and optical flow), distinguishing it from prior methods that require supervised 3D bounding boxes or panoptic labels [14964-suds.md]. Unlike object-centric approaches like NSG, SUDS handles ego-motion and multi-video representations without linear memory growth relative to the number of videos [14964-suds.md].
+### [SUDS](14964-suds.md)
+SUDS is a 4D neural representation for large-scale dynamic urban scenes that factorizes the scene into three separate hash table data structures to efficiently encode static, dynamic, and far-field radiance fields. It solves the problem of scaling neural reconstruction to city-level environments with tens of thousands of objects and ego-motion across multiple videos by using unlabeled target signals (RGB, sparse LiDAR, 2D descriptors, 2D optical flow) for supervision. Unlike sibling methods that rely on supervised 3D bounding boxes or panoptic labels, SUDS disentangles dynamic objects from the static background and models shadow effects without manual annotation, enabling free-viewpoint rendering, semantic decomposition, and 3D scene flow estimation.
+[SUDS](14964-suds.md)
 
-### CCNeRF
-CCNeRF is a neural field representation that enables efficient compression and composition of 3D scenes by learning a hybrid tensor rank decomposition of the scene without using neural networks for rendering [15008-ccnerf.md]. Unlike NeRF variants that rely on a shared MLP renderer (e.g., NSVF) or hybrid tensor-MLP approaches (e.g., TensoRF), CCNeRF models the radiance field *only* with tensor rank decomposition, preserving low-rank approximation properties to allow dynamic model size adjustment via rank truncation and arbitrary composition via rank concatenation [15008-ccnerf.md].
+### [CCNeRF](15008-ccnerf.md)
+CCNeRF is a neural field representation that enables efficient compression and composition of 3D scenes by learning a hybrid tensor rank decomposition of the scene without using neural networks for rendering. Unlike NeRF variants that rely on a shared MLP renderer (e.g., NSVF) or TensoRF which uses MLPs that prevent direct compression/composition, CCNeRF models the field *only* with tensor rank decomposition, allowing arbitrary composition without retraining and dynamic model size adjustment via rank truncation.
